# The fitted n under load, which is what the factor is read off: factor = n(k=1) / n(k).
#
# Every unit gets its own k=1 arm here rather than borrowing the table's n, so the ratio is between
# two measurements taken the same way in the same session -- the table's rows were measured at 30 s
# a point and these at 90, and the fixed arms have already shown the lite row to be marginal at the
# longer point. A factor read across two different methods would not be a factor.
#
# --start is deliberately well below the expected fit: the bench's bisection only narrows between a
# n that fitted and one that did not, so a --start that misses on its first probe reports no fitted
# n at all. At k=5 a Full model costs about twice what it costs alone, so 16 would have missed.
bisect | full-fit-k1   | 1 | 25 |  8 |  32 | --unit nam --model "$M/NAM Ampeg VT-40/Ampeg VT-40 - Vol 4, Bass 6, Mid 5, Treble 8, M160.nam" --slim 1.0
bisect | full-fit-k2   | 2 | 25 |  8 |  32 | --unit nam --model "$M/NAM Ampeg VT-40/Ampeg VT-40 - Vol 4, Bass 6, Mid 5, Treble 8, M160.nam" --slim 1.0
